![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

This logic can be simplified by using a mutable `buildMode` variable and performing the check directly. This allows Dart's flow analysis to promote `sanitizer` to a non-nullable type, eliminating the need for the null assertion operator (`!`).

```dart
    var buildMode = buildOptions.buildMode;
    if (sanitizer != null && buildMode == BuildModeEnum.fetch) {
      buildMode = BuildModeEnum.checkout;
      stdout.writeln(
        'boring: building from source, because there are no prebuilt '
        'libraries with the ${sanitizer.name} sanitizer.',
      );
    }
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. Avoid adding redundant null checks when preconditions or surrounding logic already guarantee that the property or variable is non-null.
</details>

